{"xson":[{"/iati-activities/iati-activity":[{"/activity-date":[{"@iso-date":"2016-09-22","@type":"2"},{"@iso-date":"2024-06-30","@type":"4"}],"/activity-status@code":"4","/collaboration-type@code":"2","/contact-info":[{"/organisation/narrative":[{"1":"International Fund for Agricultural Development","@xml:lang":"EN"}],"/person-name/narrative":[{"1":"Habte Selassie, Dagmawi","@xml:lang":"EN"}],"/telephone":[{"1":"+390654591"}],"/website":[{"1":"http://www.ifad.org"}],"@type":"1"}],"/default-aid-type":[{"@code":"C01","@vocabulary":"1"}],"/default-tied-status@code":"5","/description":[{"/narrative":[{"1":"The specific objectives will aim at the following: (I) Sustainably intensify dairy production and productivity among participating smallholder farmers. This shall be achieved through the promotion of improved climate-smart dairy farming practices and access to quality dairy inputs, extension services including veterinary and AI services; appropriate green technologies, as well as business and financial services, following a hub model approach.\n\n(ii) Increase incomes by at least 80% among participating smallholder farmers from dairy farming through a combined effect of the increased milk production and improved market access. This shall be achieved through the development of 30 dairy hubs; establishment and strengthening of dairy farmer organizations; and facilitation of linkages to markets and dairy value chain actors, such as milk collectors, processors, transporters, traders, and investors in milk quality through public-private-producer partnerships (4Ps).","@xml:lang":"EN"}]}],"/document-link":[{"/category":[{"@code":"A02"},{"@code":"A07"},{"@code":"A08"}],"/language":[{"@code":"EN"}],"/title/narrative":[{"1":"Rwanda 2000001195: RDDP Supervision Report April 2023","@xml:lang":"EN"}],"@format":"APPLICATION/PDF","@url":"https://operations.ifad.org/documents/654016/8ea5a39f-3fe6-458c-8051-c8638ebbba75"},{"/category":[{"@code":"A02"},{"@code":"A07"},{"@code":"A08"}],